--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -8,6 +8,20 @@ package, not for somebody reading this repository's commit log.
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Changed
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` now validates every tool call's `input` against the tool's declared JSON Schema
+  `inputSchema` before invoking the executor, compiling static schemas once at `register` time (throwing
+  synchronously if a schema cannot be compiled) and caching function-produced schemas by reference. Calls
+  that fail `required`, declared property `type`, `enum`, or an explicit `additionalProperties: false`
+  check return a `ToolResponse` describing the failing field paths and constraints (without echoing or
+  logging offending property values) instead of throwing, so the model can self-correct within
+  `maxToolRounds`; undeclared extra properties still pass through unchanged unless the schema forbids them,
+  with no type coercion or injected defaults. **Migration:** executors that previously hand-validated
+  `input` now receive only arguments their `inputSchema` already accepts, and any tool that relied on
+  seeing malformed input to return its own custom error string will no longer be invoked on schema-invalid
+  calls.
+
